ive levels of  second sourcing  or dual sourcing the first level is uh  is market screening and that's simply  that we've identified potential  alternative suppliers  level two is a supplier evaluation where  sourcing look at the supplier to see  that they're  feasible uh in terms of meeting our  standards and our requirements  level three is material evaluation  conducted by  r d which is a document  analysis of the feasibility of the  materials that  would be supplied by a potential  supplier in level 4 we've done  full r d testing and  that bench scale to validate the raw  material  delivery and performance and in level  five we've fully implemented  the second source and the reason we have  different levels is because our aim  is to reduce the transfer lead time that  is reduce the risk  and reduce the time it will take us to  implement the second source  but at the same time minimize the change  control burden  as far as our customers are concerned  so when it comes to trying to position  ourselves for success in uncertain times  when the code of 19 pandemic started to  impact our business  some of the what some of the risk  mitigation plans were already underway  so we had already reviewed the article  data stored in our erp system to ensure  it was accurate we had the  correct lead times and inventory  values and so on and so forth we started  a program to look at short-term  risk mitigation initiatives and this was  focused very much on  raising raw material inventory and  including vendor managed  inventory and we'd also started a  project to increase the number of  multiple sources  and multiple manufacturing options with  the same source  that we had for our high risk raw  materials  and in this in addition to that we  continued with our open communication  and having a clear  change notification process with both  suppliers  and customers we continue uh with our  fairly uh rigorous auto supply auditing  program but we had a review of the  buying strategy